    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d801">

                <pb facs="0852" n="838" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg838"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.21112 RP/48: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-03-03T12:00:00-05:00">March 3,
                            1944—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 4:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>393. See my A–178, February 26, noon. This morning Folsom, Rubin<anchor n="96"
                        xml:id="d801-f1"/> and I had meeting with Minister of Education who has been
                    designated by Acting President Echandía to deal with replacement <pb facs="0853"
                        n="839" xml:id="pg839"/> program. Dr. Rocha said that as Minister of
                    Hacienda and Minister of Public Health<anchor n="97" xml:id="d801-f2"/> are
                    leaving office next week to enter presidential campaign administrative action
                    with regard to nationalization of German drug industry probably cannot take
                    place until early April. On the return of Derby<anchor n="98" xml:id="d801-f3"/>
                    from Mexico City however Dr. Rocha indicated willingness to discuss matter with
                    him and it was suggested by me that Folsom and Rubin stop in Bogotá on their
                    return trip from Chile to acquaint themselves more fully with situation.</p>
                <p>Dr. Rocha made it clear that because of the political situation no constructive
                    steps may be expected for some weeks.</p>
                <p>Rocha said that the question of replacement program would have to be submitted to
                    the National Defense Commission prior to administrative action being taken by
                    the Minister of Hacienda.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lane</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
